Feature: Update Resource Type

  Background:
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: update Resource Type with all required fields.
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Update",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Update",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: update Resource Type with description: null
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": null,
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": null,
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: update Resource Type with description: empty
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: update Resource Type with an existing/duplicate key but with different project
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 2",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "Project-2-Updated",
         "description": "Project 2 Updated",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Project 2 Updated",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: update Resource Type with description: blank (whitespace)
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: update Resource Type with tags
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "FAQ-Updated-1",
            "FAQ-Updated-2"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "FAQ-Updated-1",
            "FAQ-Updated-2"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type with name: null
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": null,
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 400
    And the response body includes status 400 and error message 'Bad Request'

  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type with name: blank
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 400
    And the response body includes status 400 and error message 'Bad Request'

  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type with actions: null and empty
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": []
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 400
    And the response body includes status 400 and error message 'Bad Request'

  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type with actions: null
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": null
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 400
    And the response body includes status 400 and error message 'Bad Request'

  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type with actions: contains duplicate value
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 400
    And the response body includes status 400 and error message 'Bad Request'

  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type by a non-existent Key
    Given the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'Wrong_Key' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 404
    And the response body includes status 404 and error message 'Not Found'

  Scenario: Positive: Update Resource Type to delete any action value that is not used by a policy
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-1",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY-1",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ-1",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """
    And the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ-1' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-1",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: Update Resource Type with same Action values but in different order
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-2",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY-2",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ-2",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """
    And the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ-2' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "actions": [
            "delete",
            "update",
            "create",
            "view"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type updated successfully with response code 200
    And return the updated resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-2",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: Update Resource Type to add any values in resource actions
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-3",
