  Scenario: Negative: update Resource Type when the actions are Used by Policy
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-FU",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY_FAILS_UPDATE",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ-FU",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """
    And the Resource Admin with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' wants to update the Resource Type 'FAQ-FU' with the following attributes:
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-FU",
         "name": "FAQ-Updated",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "create",
            "delete",
            "download"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin updates the Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type update fails with response code 409
    And the response body includes status 409 and error message 'Conflict'
